            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "The Olofsborg apartment house in the Katajanokka neighborhood in Helsinki was built in 1902 and designed by Gesellius, Lindgren, &amp; Saarinen architects.  It is located at Katajanokankatu 1 (Skatuddsgatan 1) / Kauppiaankatu 7 (Köpmansgatan 7). The towers of the building are inspired by the Olavinlinna Castle in Savonlinna, which is called Olofsborg in Swedish. In 2007, Olofsborg was second runner-up in a public vote for the most beautiful Jugendstil (Art Nouveau) building in Helsinki sponsored by the newspaper Helsingin Sanomat.",
              "source": "commons-desc-page"
